wmcliphist: history in the database of big-wm-clipboard

Big WindowMaker keeps one clipboard history for both sessions, with a
Super+V window (search, favorites, retention) and a SQLite database that
survives reboots. wmcliphist, the X11 dockapp, records each new copy there
(through `big-wm-clipboard --store`, content on a pipe, never on a command
line), starts with the saved history, keeps the lock of an item as a
favorite and reloads its menu on SIGUSR2 (sent when the window deletes or
clears items). Ignore actions of ~/.wmcliphistrc are respected. Without
big-wm-clipboard installed nothing changes.

